{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Her foes became</b> — each one a head, and likewise: \"the daughters of song shall trouble it\" — each one of them." "<b>are at ease</b> — from the root of שלוה." "<b>is in turmoil</b> — from the heavy stem [hithpa'el], added from יגון, and likewise: \"my soul is in turmoil\"." "<b>went into captivity</b> — with omission of bet, like \"found in the house of YHWH\"."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {3 "The comparison is to 2 Chronicles 34:32 (הנמצא בית ה'), where bet is likewise absent before the noun; here Ibn Ezra reads שבי as construct to a following noun with the prepositional bet omitted."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:24.440482240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}